<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Prima H1 net up 41.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Singapore Prima H1 net up 41.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>	    (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>				     1996		1995</p>
<p>    Net profit		   9.58     vs	6.79</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)     25.60     vs     18.10</p>
<p>    Dividend   (percent)    10.0	vs     10.0</p>
<p>    Turnover		    60.86     vs     60.97</p>
<p>    Interest income	    4.57     vs	4.85</p>
<p>    Interest payment	   1.94     vs	2.88</p>
<p>    Depreciation		 4.47     vs	4.14</p>
<p>    Pretax profit		2.83     vs	2.76</p>
<p>    Minorities (gain)	  0.99     vs	0.75</p>
<p>    Div register/Div payable   Sept 24/October 8</p>
<p>NOTE: Prima Ltd, a diversified flour milling company, said high grain prices continued to affect selling prices of wheat flour affecting the sales and profit levels of the company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
